ps://x.com/i/broadcasts/2YREXZXlegmVPa", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119852536178135040/DGoE9geK?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119852536178135040/DGoE9geK?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 259, "status": 200, "title": "IMF", "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/broadcasts/2YREXZXlegmVPa", "url": "https://t.co/rtjwn4D5gb"}]}, "id": "2119852532029919379", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 13634, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Join us at #ARCPolak on Nov 13 at 1:30pm ET for this year’s policy panel “How Will the World Become Multipolar: Managing Transition Risks and Seizing New Opportunities” with @STenreyroIMF, Haibin Zhu, Maurice Obstfeld, @YaredPierre &amp; @RBI’s Poonam Gupta. https://t.co/rtjwn4D5gb", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2119852532029919379"}, {"author_id": "1161370756208648193", "created_at": "2026-11-09T17:44:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119848520047812842"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 107, "start": 98, "tag": "FEDSNote"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/u-s-private-credit-vehicles-institutional-structure-and-aggregate-balance-sheets-20261109.html", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119848521352314880/iwn0Eiud?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119848521352314880/iwn0Eiud?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "U.S. Private Credit Vehicles: Institutional Structure and Aggregate Balance Sheets", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/u-s-private-credit-vehicles-institutional-structure-and-aggregate-balance-sheets-20261109.html", "url": "https://t.co/WQpcDzV8Q0"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/duabn5piOJ", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2119848520047812842/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119848300773810176", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/duabn5piOJ"}]}, "id": "2119848520047812842", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 48, "impression_count": 5304, "like_count": 67, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "Following our first note, “Introducing Private Credit into the U.S. Financial Accounts,” this new #FEDSNote details the methodology and how leverage and portfolio concentration differ across vehicles, reflecting distinct institutional structures. (1/2) https://t.co/WQpcDzV8Q0 https://t.co/duabn5piOJ", "url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2119848520047812842"}, {"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-11-09T17:23:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119843249980662241"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/spisallyouneed…", "end": 308, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/spisallyouneed/status/2119829366758604963", "start": 285, "url": "https://t.co/kNROfQcCMw"}]}, "id": "2119843249980662241", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 638, "impression_count": 77510, "like_count": 759, "quote_count": 12, "reply_count": 77, "retweet_count": 41}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119829366758604963", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Sam and his team are working on a super exciting idea: autonomous businesses. \n\nAcquiring distressed or stagnant SaaS apps and handing the keys to an agent harness is the ultimate real-world eval. Just P&amp;L as the objective function and the market as the feedback signal.\n\nCongrats https://t.co/kNROfQcCMw", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2119843249980662241"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-09T17:09:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119839803424563557"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "IMF Reaches Staff-Level Agreement on the Sixth Review under Ecuador’s Extended Fund Facility Arrangement and on the Resilience and Sustainability Facility Arrangement", "display_url": "imf.org/en/news/articl…", "end": 273, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2026/11/08/26256-ecuador-sla-6th-review", "images": [{"height": 405, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119783548739518464/CQVvkbHM?format=png&name=orig", "width": 400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119783548739518464/CQVvkbHM?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 250, "status": 200, "title": "IMF Reaches Staff-Level Agreement on the Sixth Review under Ecuador’s Extended Fund Facility Arrangement and on the Resilience and Sustainability Facility Arrangement", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2026/11/08/26256-ecuador-sla-6th-review", "url": "https://t.co/iTI2zx22Uh"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mevnylUUW5", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2119839803424563557/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119839793853206528", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/mevnylUUW5"}]}, "id": "2119839803424563557", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 16949, "like_count": 63, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Ecuador's economic program continues to perform strongly. IMF staff and the authorities agreed on next steps, including reforms to support growth, investment and jobs, and about US$710 million to strengthen resilience, subject to IMF Board approval. https://t.co/iTI2zx22Uh https://t.co/mevnylUUW5", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2119839803424563557"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-09T17:02:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119837930050986340"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 263, "start": 255, "tag": "economy"}, {"end": 272, "start": 264, "tag": "markets"}], "mentions": [{"end": 280, "id": "61559439", "start": 273, "username": "nvidia"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/sZsNRGlYpW", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119837930050986340/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119837927018532864", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/sZsNRGlYpW"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/sZsNRGlYpW", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119837930050986340/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119837927010172929", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/sZsNRGlYpW"}]}, "id": "2119837930050986340", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 39837, "like_count": 291, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 44, "retweet_count": 35}, "text": "Given Nvidia’s role in tech, this combination (Nasdaq up 2.4% and Nvidia down 5.8%) seemed highly unlikely before today.\nIt signals strong dip-buying investor appetite across the sector, coupled with market optimism that Nvidia’s issues remain contained.\n#economy #markets @nvidia https://t.co/sZsNRGlYpW", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119837930050986340"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-11-09T16:33:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119830736979239286"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 92, "start": 84, "tag": "BLSData"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Doctor’s appointments (for ourselves, our family, and our pets), school functions, errands—occasionally workers need to take an hour or two off during work hours. Whatever", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 116, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/ease-of-taking-time-off-during-the-workday-varied-by-sex-and-educational-attainment.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119830740741529608/MUHo9BQu?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119830740741529608/MUHo9BQu?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 93, "status": 200, "title": "Ease of taking time off during the workday varied by sex and educational attainment : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/ease-of-taking-time-off-during-the-workday-varied-by-sex-and-educational-attainment.htm", "url": "https://t.co/6h2UJSpQ31"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/XB8qjKOBIu", "end": 140, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2119830736979239286/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119830306190479360", "start": 117, "url": "https://t.co/XB8qjKOBIu"}]}, "id": "2119830736979239286", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2923, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Ease of taking time off during the workday varied by sex and educational attainment #BLSData https://t.co/6h2UJSpQ31 https://t.co/XB8qjKOBIu", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2119830736979239286"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-09T16:28:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119829445980623124"], "id": "2119829445980623124", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 11240, "like_count": 56, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "BLS didn't publish CPI in October 2025 due to the shutdown and as a result won't publish 12-month changes tomorrow.\n\nMy tentative plan is to publish 12-month numbers using an interpolated index for October 2025 (the geometric average of Sep and Nov).\n\nWhat are others doing?", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2119829445980623124"}, {"author_id": "15072071", "created_at": "2026-11-09T16:11:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119825280063647916"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "NEW YORK—The Federal Reserve Bank of New York’s Center for Microeconomic Data today released the October 2026 Survey of Consumer Expectations, which shows that households’ inflation expectations remained unchanged at the short-, medium-, and longer-term horizons. Labor market expectations were mixed with unemployment and job loss expectations deteriorating, while job finding expectations improved. Expectations of an increase in unemployment reached the highest level since April 2020. Conversely, job", "display_url": "nyfed.org/4zUiuXH", "end": 199, "expanded_url": "https://nyfed.org/4zUiuXH", "start": 176, "status": 200, "title": "Inflation Expectations Stable; Labor Market Expectations Mixed - FEDERAL RESERVE BANK of NEW YORK", "unwound_url": "https://www.newyorkfed.org/newsevents/news/research/2026/20261109", "url": "https://t.co/NmK29wVlT5"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/lKBbQdV1sN", "end": 223, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2119825280063647916/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119825269758242817", "start": 200, "url": "https://t.co/lKBbQdV1sN"}]}, "id": "2119825280063647916", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2706, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Our October 2026 Survey of Consumer Expectations shows that households’ inflation expectations remained unchanged at the short-, medium-, and longer-term horizons. Learn more:\nhttps://t.co/NmK29wVlT5 https://t.co/lKBbQdV1sN", "url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2119825280063647916"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "26538229", "name": "Federal Reserve", "username": "federalreserve"}, {"id": "1161370756208648193", "name": "FedResearch", "username": "FedResearch"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}, {"id": "59603406", "name": "Nick Timiraos", "username": "NickTimiraos"}, {"id": "15072071", "name": "New York Fed", "username": "NewYorkFed"}, {"id": "33261737